#====================================================================
# Draft: raw Makefile link step hardcodes `gcc`; generate() provides a
#        gcc->clang wrapper on PATH so make works where only clang exists
#        (kevlar 2.0.1)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-kevlar-2.0.1-gcc-wrapper-for-makefile
trigger_tool:           make|gcc|clang|conan
phase:                  linking|compilation
error_signature:        make: gcc: No such file or directory|gcc: not found|Error 127.*gcc|md2html target.*gcc

severity:               2
category:               build-system, makefile, toolchain, conan
match_keywords:         raw makefile, Makefile, gcc, clang, hardcoded compiler, wrapper, PATH, md2html, conan, generate, CI no gcc, link step

title:                  Raw Makefile link step hardcodes `gcc`; generate() provides a gcc->clang wrapper on PATH so make works where only clang exists

root_cause:             Some raw (non-autotools/cmake/meson) makefiles hardcode the compiler binary name in specific link rules (e.g. `gcc ... -o bin/md2html`) in addition to a CC variable. The OHOS CI/toolchain environment provides clang but not gcc, so only that target fails with `make: gcc: No such file or directory` while other targets built via $(CC) succeed. Passing CC=clang on the make command line does not fix hardcoded occurrences.

affected_scope:         Any Conan recipe whose upstream makefile contains a hardcoded `gcc` (or other absent compiler) in a target rule, built in an environment without that binary. Verified instance - kevlar-2.0.1 makefile md2html target (raw makefile, no configure).

verification_cmd:       PATH="<build>/bin:$PATH" make CC=clang all within conan create; the previously failing target links successfully.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           generate-gcc-wrapper-in-private-prefix
rec_description:        In conanfile generate(), create a private build-folder bin/ dir containing a `gcc` wrapper script `#!/bin/sh\nexec <CC> "$@"` (resolving <CC> from the Conan toolchain conf `tools.build:compiler_executables` dict's "c" key — R33 forbids relying on shell env vars like ${CC}; fall back to shutil.which("clang") only if the conf is empty), chmod +x it, and prepend that dir to PATH when running make. Keeps the injection in the build folder only (R49: no shared /usr/local pollution; the compiler id comes from the Conan toolchain).
rec_command:            generate(): read compilers = self.conf.get("tools.build:compiler_executables", default={}, check_type=dict); cc = compilers.get("c") or shutil.which("clang"); write build_folder/bin/gcc wrapper -> cc; build(): PATH="<build>/bin:$PATH" make CC=<cc> CFLAGS=... all
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/k/kevlar/2.0.1/conanfile.py (generate() + build())

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-makefile-link-rule
fallback_description:   Patch the makefile link rule to use $(CC) instead of the hardcoded gcc (upstream fix). Cleaner long-term but touches upstream build files and needs a patch per version; the wrapper approach keeps the upstream tree pristine.
fallback_command:       replace `gcc $(objs) -o bin/md2html` with `$(CC) $(objs) -o bin/md2html` via patch
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       write wrapper into /usr/local|/usr/bin|SYS_PREFIX|os.access(X_OK) probing|export CC=gcc|symlink into shared dirs
forbid_1_reason:        R49 forbids shared-prefix injection (worker file systems are shared and polluted); X_OK probing fails under HMDFS because chmod is ignored.
forbid_1_consequence:   PF6 preflight rejection and cross-worker pollution.

principles:             minimal-patch, private-prefix-injection, toolchain-from-conan, real-evidence-over-assumption